<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan tenders for 200,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Pakistan tenders for 200,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1996-10-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan tendered on Saturday for 200,000 tonnes of U.S. soft white wheat under the U.S. GSM-102 credit programme for November 12-30 delivery, the Food and Agriculture Ministry said.  </p>
<p>The ministry said in a tender notice that bids should be submitted by November 3 and would be opened at 11 a.m. (0600 GMT) the same day.</p>
<p>-- Islamabad newsroom 9251-274757</p>
</text>
